{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9e5a93d2de56142312fcab7a2701591ea6514c8e79f6d0c0bc4510717fa5f09c", "source_text": "The base change of a morphism which is locally of finite type\nis locally of finite type. The same is true for morphisms of\nfinite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:53b6dd437813acb98f734c0991be948d007c5d5e7a9ae561fc3e17b3d213d9d1", "unit_id": "tag:01T4:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-type-characterize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-type-P}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-base-change-finiteness}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-preserved-base-change}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e3479efa42efb9e9a62d675b7aa3e5d22cc51b9dbdae32dd9f178f83690fad29", "source_text": "In the proof of Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe saw that being of finite type is a local property of ring maps.\nHence the first statement of the lemma follows from\nLemma <REF_0002> combined\nwith the fact that being of finite type is a property of ring maps that is\nstable under base change, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nBy the above and the fact that a base change of a\nquasi-compact morphism is quasi-compact, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0004>\nwe see that the base change of a morphism of finite type is\na morphism of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1610966ffd7ec6535e4964c98a8fe6ef5d3090bcdb9fa8acb6006ddfb340ae32", "unit_id": "tag:01T4:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-immersion-locally-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cf4db088a6b9cf414a5ecace5f2ea7dc52a42d86bf90adf1a19fdaed104536b9", "source_text": "A closed immersion is of finite type.\nAn immersion is locally of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:923b8cdff896d77564bc62a5c024d622e11b48b5376b18dde3416fe85be243fa", "unit_id": "tag:01T5:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7a17ef56426a8134767d04b2df47d80b3e2e8e8aaab51501491627c02360e7f9", "source_text": "This is true because an open immersion is a local isomorphism,\nand a closed immersion is obviously of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7201a3e9df2eff08d8434d81f92aa82d65ba67ae2fffc664f105f265e7862af8", "unit_id": "tag:01T5:proof"}
